# Code Style: Staircase Formatting

- Follow existing repository formatting first. If there is no clear local precedent, use rules below.
- Prefer multiline "staircase" layout for long imports, object literals, arrays, function params, and JSX props.
- In multiline structures, keep one item/property per line.
- Keep trailing commas in multiline lists and objects.
- Use consistent indentation and avoid mixing compact and expanded styles in one block.

## Imports

Use multiline grouped imports when there are many symbols or lines become hard to scan.

```typescript
import {
    BottomSheetView,
    BottomSheetModal,
    BottomSheetBackdrop,
    BottomSheetBackdropProps,
} from '@gorhom/bottom-sheet';
```

## Objects and arrays

Prefer expanded layout for nested or medium/large structures.

```typescript
const payload = {
    email: values.email,
    profile: {
        lastName: user.lastName,
        firstName: user.firstName,
    },
    tags: [
        'account',
        'settings',
    ],
};
```

## JSX props

When there are multiple props, put each prop on its own line.

```tsx
<Button
    disabled={!dirty}
    variant="outline"
    title="CHANGE EMAIL"
    onPress={handleSubmit}
/>
```
